<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34973" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνᾰρα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ων</span>, τά, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐναίρω</span>) only
		pl., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>arms and trappings of a
				slain foe, spoils</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φέρειν ἔ. βροτόεντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.480
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φέρομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					8.534
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλλ᾽ ἔ. Τρώων</span>
			<i>taken from</i> them, <i><span class="en">
				13.268
			</span></i>; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. βροτόεντα Δόλωνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					10.570
				</span></i>
			: generally, <i>spoil, booty</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν</span> [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φόρμιγγα</span>] 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρετ᾽ ἐξ ἐνάρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.188
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				6.68
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				367
			</span></i>.--
				Ep.
			 word (used by <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				177
			</span></i> (lyr.)) for Trag. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκῦλα,
			λάφυρα</span>.</div>
